WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.167
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.367
We're about to play a
mind-blowing game.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:08.334
But, first, I'm going to need
someone to play against.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:09.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:13.033
Her new movie, "Amsterdam,"
is in theaters October 7th.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.934
Please welcome the one-and-only
Margot Robbie!

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.834
-Thanks, guys. Thank you.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:23.434
I want you to know that
I am only doing this

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.734
because it's your birthday.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.467
-I love you.
Thank you for doing this.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:31.701
We're about to face off in a
game called "Blow Your Mind."

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:32.868
-♪ Blow ♪

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:37.501
♪ Blow your mind ♪

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:41.033
-Questlove -- Questlove,
do you want to explain

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.367
how the game works?

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.701
[ Hissing ]

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.267
-[ Echoing ] Yes, Jimmy.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:52.167
In this game, I will read each
a mind-blowing fact.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:56.501
And you must decide
if that fact is true or false.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:01:02.901
If you choose wrong,
we will blow...your...mind.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:08.234
And you will blasted in the face
from the tube in front of you.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.501
Make the right choice, and your
opponent gets their mind blown.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.000
-Okay.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.000
-The first fact is for Margot.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.767
True or false?

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.834
-There are more what?
-McDonald's.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:27.067
-There are more McDonald's
in the U.S. than libraries.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.701
-I would say that's true.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.734
[ Music intensifies ]

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:37.100
-The answer may surprise you.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.133
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.267
It's false.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.100
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.200
What?!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.701
-What just happened to me?

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.133
-Can we please see that --
No, silence, silence!

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.400
Can we see that in slow motion?

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.300
-Oh, my God.
This game is intense.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.601
-Wait. Something
went over your head.

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.167
I don't know what it was.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.501
I think it was feathers.
Alright.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:02.868
-Jimmy.
-Yes?

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.434
-The next fact is for you.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.467
True or false?

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.667
True or false?

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.901
-How did she get
more McDonald's or libraries?

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:17.100
An ostrich's eye
is bigger than their brain?

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.300
-True or false, Jimmy?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.701
-I understand,
but let me think for a second.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.601
An ostrich's eye --
I don't even know how big an --

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.801
-True or false?

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:26.634
-I know, I know, I know
it's true or false.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:27.767
-They're such big animals.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.767
-Yes, but they have tiny heads.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.501
-Birds often have small brains.
I don't know why I'm helping.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:35.601
-I'm going to say false.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:37.434
-The answer may surprise you.

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:38.667
-No, please.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.767
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:48.701
-It's true, Jimmy.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.467
Can we please see
that again in slow motion?

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:55.100
-What flew -- what flew on you?
-What in the hell was...

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.734
What was that? Was that lettuce?

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.667
-Do you have lettuce on you?

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:03.934
What -- How did --
It was lettuce?

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.067
-Your wig is doing
something special.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.667
-You got feathers,
and I got raw lettuce.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.901
-Is that what I got?
-Yeah, you did.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.701
Margot...
-Okay.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.000
-...you're up next.
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.901
-True or false, Margot?
-Yes, Questlove?

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.534
-False.

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:35.000
-Margot, the answer
may surprise you.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.033
-May, surprise you, yeah.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.701
-Oh, dear God!
[ Ding ]

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:49.167
-Can we -- can we please see
that again in slow motion?

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.400
-What even came -- Just air.
-What came out?

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.300
-Oh, Ping-Pong balls?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.000
Ping-Pong balls
just hit my face.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.667
Who's loading up my cannon,

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.167
and who's loading up
Margot's cannon?

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.300
-I am.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.901
-You can't shoot
Ping-Pong balls at me.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.300
This is ridiculous. Alright.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.834
-The next fact is for Jimmy.
-Yep.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:07.868
-Jimmy.
-Yes.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:11.434
-True or...Jimmy?
-Yes?

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:15.033
[ Laughter ]
-True or false?

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:21.934
True or false?

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.667
-I mean, if I'm in
the pineapple business,

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.601
I mean, I've got to
call Dole on this.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:28.901
Pineapples take five years --
that seems...

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.701
-And they take no time
at all to eat.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:31.968
-...impossible.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:35.133
But there's a lot of layers
to a pineapple.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:37.734
-True or false, Jimmy?
-Yeah, I know, I know, I know.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:40.167
Yeah.
-That's hard.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.934
-Pineapples take
five years to grow.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.434
I'm going to say that is --

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.834
-I mean, you grow a baby
in nine months.

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:51.234
You can't, like...

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.033
-Five years to grow.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.334
I'm gonna say that's --
that is false.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:59.200
-Jimmy, the answer --
-The answer may surprise you.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.901
-Yes, exactly.

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.100
[ Ding ]

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.234
-Pineapples take
two to three years to grow.

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.901
Let's see that again
in slow motion.

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:17.901
-Watch your --

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:21.400
Your cannon is going over
your -- One stuck on your nose.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.467
Okay, good.
-What hit me?

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:25.434
[ Thunder crashes ]
-It's -- Uh-oh.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:30.133
-Hey, that sound means it's time
for the final question.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.567
And it comes with a twist.

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.701
If you answer incorrectly,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:40.100
both of your minds
will be blown.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ooh!

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.734
Wait. Did he just say we're
both getting our minds --

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.133
-Yes, both.
-Gotcha.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:50.934
-Margot,
this conundrum is for you.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:01.467
-Look at my hair.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.234
-Everything else
was true or false.

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:05.100
Why is --
What color is a mirror?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.100
-What -- I feel like --
-Margot, what color is a mirror?

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.667
-Silver?

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:12.100
-What did you say?
-Silver?

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.901
-Silver?

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.167
Yeah.

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:17.968
-Maybe reflect...

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.434
-Well, guess what.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:22.601
-The answer may surprise you.
-The answer may surprise you.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.467
-I bet it will. I bet it will.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:30.801
-You are wrong.

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:34.667
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:36.367
Let's see that in slow motion.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:38.100
-What's the answer?

00:06:43.501 --> 00:06:45.634
Margot Robbie, everybody!
-Thanks, guys.

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:46.968
-Margot Robbie, everybody!

